{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "Runtime mood light for the SITE-7 background plates (site7_room_art_layer.gd, site7_mood.gd). The v2 plates are painted under one neutral light so their seams match; each room's mood is added here instead. Per mission: a grade over every plate and the abyss backdrop behind the level (site7_abyss_backdrop.gd). Per room plate: its ambient grade (connectors turn from one room's grade to the other's along the deck), lamp pools (the plate's painted lamps, found by tools/environment/build_site7_mood_light.py into site7_mood_lamps.json), an overhead fill over the middle of its floor and extra lights. Every listed plate's flat outer void is see-through (site7_void_masks.json) unless \"void\": false. Robot and operator art is never lit or tinted.",
  "units": "exposure: stops. tint: RGB balance, normalised to keep luminance. saturation: factor around luminance. Lamp and light radius: world px (floor ellipse, half as tall). strength: added to the light multiplier at the pool centre. pulse: [hz, depth]. at: plate texture coordinates. fill reach: radius as a share of the floor's larger side. abyss colours: 0-1 RGB.",
